            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>The disclosure relates to a biomimetic implant for spinal cord or nerve injury, the implant comprising: a three-dimensional (3D) printed implant body comprising: a first end and a second end formed in a biomimetic shape which mimics structure of a nerve or spinal cord injury site as to host axon organization; and a plurality of linear channels within the body originating at the first end and terminating at the second end, wherein the plurality of linear channels retain their pre-implantation structure for at least 4 weeks in vivo.</p>
            </abstract>
